From 72fbba3d20f4616d7312b5e2b7f79daf6e82f2fa Fri Mar 13 11:11:00 2026
From: Valentyna Khomits <vkhomits@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Mar 2026 11:11:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Create protobuf systemlib patch for TensorFlow

Creates protobuf_systemlib.patch applied to the TensorFlow archive during
the Bazel build. Replaces the vendored protobuf download with a
jaxlib-style repo from conda's protobuf-bazel-rules package, plus the
systemlib BUILD files protobuf-bazel-rules and system grpc need.

Does not touch the TF archive's .bazelrc or WORKSPACE: Bazel never reads
those for a downloaded repo. proto_bazel_features is registered from
tensorflow-text's WORKSPACE (patch 0007).

Only the copies tensorflow-text's WORKSPACE actually evaluates are
patched: @org_tensorflow's third_party/py/python_init_rules.bzl (which
creates @com_google_protobuf) and tensorflow/workspace2.bzl (grpc
systemlib links). XLA's python_init_rules.bzl/workspace2.bzl are never
loaded here, and tf_workspace2()'s maybe(com_google_protobuf) is skipped
because python_init_rules() already defined it.

LLVM_SHA256 in xla/third_party/llvm/workspace.bzl is pinned to the
re-compressed archive variant GitHub currently serves (00b1077e...), the
one build.sh fetches into --distdir; TF's upstream pin (3f986184...) no
longer matches what codeload returns.
